<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · region</p><h1 class="enc-title">Hazarajat</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Hazarajat is the mountainous central region of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/afghanistan">Afghanistan</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/bantustan">homeland</a> of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/hazara">Hazara</a> people, centred on Bamiyan and the highlands of the upper Helmand. Largely self-governing until the 1890s, it was conquered by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/emir">Emir</a> <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/abdur-rahman-khan">Abdur Rahman Khan</a> in brutal campaigns between 1891 and 1893, in which many Hazaras were killed, enslaved or driven from their land.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/hazarajat.jpg" alt="Hazarajat" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Niazof · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Hazaristan_(orthographic_projection).png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
